blocks.english:
The Virgin encloses God in her womb;
Enclosed, he rejoices at the Enclosed One
From the keeping of the womb;
Gestures serve as speech,
While the silent wonders
Of infants now converse.

The fruits of marriage are given to the mother;
Now the reproach of the barren mother
Is expiated;
At the birth of so great a forerunner
Many fear, but gladness
Is the companion of fear.

He indeed was not the Light,
But that he might bear witness
To Thee, Christ, the Light;
He was not the Light, but a lamp;
Christ the Word is eternal light,
[The printed “Lucem cerans omnium” is unresolved.]

He who baptizes is raised up;
The Baptized One is not washed,
In whom there is no stain;
The waters wash, nay, are washed,
And are given power to wash
By the power of Him who cleanses all things.
